{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DU0", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:61a8d1b58635c829c0b68eb3328e8c6b8261eb372946f54ce2fa01ca30ed3ab9", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we start discussing what we can say\nabout the <ACCENT_0001>tale local structure of an algebraic stack.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f2a93c38e66cb1f5d469a0956ca1e9dfae56daa40fa9c0ee08dc8205bfa6e1db", "unit_id": "tag:0DU0:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DU0", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$Y$", "MATH_0002": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to Y$", "MATH_0005": "$R \\to U \\times_Y U$", "MATH_0006": "$X = [U/R] = U/R$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\to Y$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quotient-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8d4035d1f31a0467c6c730fb511b18e1cdc4813a8763fb4a3740d6b67d89a453", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:62645c3e53e093387572be18b02873e212ff7faafda4fed646bf7e325cd2742a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic space.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\nAssume <MATH_0004> is flat and locally of finite presentation\nand <MATH_0005> an open immersion.\nThen <MATH_0006> is an algebraic space and <MATH_0007>\nis <ACCENT_0001>tale.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ad9e4f789090e3f61dce817c7ca7b683027f84c8dfd1ec81a19c96af9b891db0", "unit_id": "tag:0DU1:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DU0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$[U/R]$", "MATH_0002": "$R \\to U \\times U$", "MATH_0003": "$U/R$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nR \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & U \\times_Y U \\ar[d] \\\\\nX \\ar[r] & X \\times_Y X\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\to X \\times_Y X$", "MATH_0008": "$X \\to Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{criteria-theorem-flat-groupoid-gives-algebraic-stack}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebraic-proposition-algebraic-stack-no-automorphisms}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{bootstrap-theorem-final-bootstrap}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{bootstrap-lemma-covering-quotient}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-flat-permanence}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{spaces-descent-lemma-flat-finitely-presented-permanence}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-check-property-covering}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-diagonal-unramified-morphism}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-unramified-flat-lfp-etale}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e7da3c86d777d5c6563e86be40fe131cbd4e0dc58db5d57074f09adfd7dd3555", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3ca9b9f2b02e2829d9e03ea5229c8d0c6a25611517085f2357ed734f68f8775d", "source_text": "The quotient stack <MATH_0001> is an algebraic stacks by\nCriteria for Representability, Theorem\n<REF_0001>.\nOn the other hand, since <MATH_0002> is a monomorphism,\nit is an algebraic space (by our abuse of language and\nAlgebraic Stacks, Proposition\n<REF_0002>)\nand of course it is equal to the algebraic space <MATH_0003>\n(of Bootstrap, Theorem <REF_0003>).\nSince <MATH_0004> is surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation\n(Bootstrap, Lemma <REF_0004>)\nwe conclude that <MATH_0005> is flat and locally of finite presentation by\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0005>\nand\nDescent on Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0006>.\nFinally, consider the cartesian diagram\n<MATH_0006>\nSince the right vertical arrow is surjective, flat, and\nlocally of finite presentation (small detail omitted), we\nfind that <MATH_0007> is an open immersion as the top horizontal arrow\nhas this property by assumption (use\nProperties of Stacks, Lemma\n<REF_0007>).\nThus <MATH_0008> is unramified by\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0008>.\nWe conclude by\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:746610d753edf63c3d6d226ae23091f1ed71c9c7371c96fc173914fa62afa195", "unit_id": "tag:0DU1:proof"}
